# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sheppard / IMU quantisation research project
#
# Rule of thumb: commit sources and documents, never build output, never
# vendor trees you did not write, never anything that can be regenerated by
# pressing a button.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- STM32CubeIDE build output ---------------------------------------------
Debug/
Release/
*.o
*.d
*.su
*.map
*.list
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.srec

# CubeIDE / Eclipse workspace state. .project and .cproject ARE committed --
# without them the project will not import.
.settings/
.metadata/
*.launch
RemoteSystemsTempFiles/

# CubeMX scratch. The .ioc IS committed: it is the source of truth for the
# pin map and peripheral configuration, and TN-16 SS1.2 exists because it was
# not read carefully enough.
.mxproject

# --- KiCad -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .history is KiCad's autosave/backup tree. It contains its own git repo with
# thousands of loose objects and must never be committed.
.history/
*-backups/
fp-info-cache
*.kicad_prl
*.bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.net
_autosave-*
*.lck

# Fabrication output is regenerated from the source files
production/
gerbers/
*.zip

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Campaign data belongs in Zenodo with a DOI, not in git. Small reference
# captures used by tests are fine; add them with `git add -f`.
Test Datasets/*
# The contents are excluded, not the directory: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so `Test Datasets/` followed by a
# negation silently does nothing.
#
# The .sdat records stay out of git (190 MB) and go to Zenodo. The analysis
# artefacts are tracked, because summary.csv is what the paper cites and what
# make_numbers.py hashes -- a deposit whose numbers cannot be traced to a
# tracked file is not one anybody can check.
*.csv
*.parquet
*.npy

# These negations must come AFTER *.csv -- the last matching rule wins, and
# an earlier negation is silently overridden.
!Test Datasets/summary.csv
!Test Datasets/plan*.txt

# --- Research corpus -------------------------------------------------------
# Unpublished findings stay out of the repository until the preprint is out.
# Anything dropped in these folders is excluded automatically.
#
# NOTE: TN-17 and TN-17A at the root ARE tracked deliberately. They document
# the firmware and are useless without it. The research notes (TN-12/13/14/16,
# literature review, concept note, manuscript drafts) live outside this folder
# and were never here to begin with -- these rules exist so that stays true
# by accident as well as by intention.
notes/
research/
corpus/
manuscript/
*.docx
*.pdf
!datasheets/**/*.pdf

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*~
*.swp

# --- Local tool state ------------------------------------------------------
.sheppard_console.json

# --- Generated figures ------------------------------------------------------
# The numbered result figures ARE tracked -- the paper references them and a
# reader cloning the repo should get them. The per-record diagnostics are build
# output of `analyse.py all` and regenerate on demand.
Figures/r[0-9]*
Figures/*_screen.png
Figures/*_overview.png
Figures/*_allan.png

# --- LaTeX build output -----------------------------------------------------
# The .tex sources and references.bib are committed. Everything below is
# regenerated by latexmk.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.fls
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.toc
paper/main.pdf
paper/sections/*.aux
paper/*.tmp
paper/*.xdv

# numbers.tex IS committed on purpose, even though make_numbers.py generates
# it. It is the provenance record linking a given PDF to a given summary.csv
# by sha256, and a reader who clones the repo must be able to build without
# first regenerating it.
